"    un administrador.\n"
"    "

msgid ""
"\n"
"Simulate use of Host-based access controls\n"
"\n"
"HBAC rules control who can access what services on what hosts and from "
"where.\n"
"You can use HBAC to control which users or groups can access a service,\n"
"or group of services, on a target host.\n"
"\n"
"Since applying HBAC rules implies use of a production environment,\n"
"this plugin aims to provide simulation of HBAC rules evaluation without\n"
"having access to the production environment.\n"
"\n"
" Test user coming to a service on a named host against\n"
" existing enabled rules.\n"
"\n"
" ipa hbactest --user= --host= --service=\n"
"              [--rules=rules-list] [--nodetail] [--enabled] [--disabled]\n"
"              [--srchost= ] [--sizelimit= ]\n"
"\n"
" --user, --host, and --service are mandatory, others are optional.\n"
"\n"
" If --rules is specified simulate enabling of the specified rules and test\n"
" the login of the user using only these rules.\n"
"\n"
" If --enabled is specified, all enabled HBAC rules will be added to "
"simulation\n"
"\n"
" If --disabled is specified, all disabled HBAC rules will be added to "
"simulation\n"
"\n"
" If --nodetail is specified, do not return information about rules matched/"
"not matched.\n"
"\n"
" If both --rules and --enabled are specified, apply simulation to --rules "
"_and_\n"
" all IPA enabled rules.\n"
"\n"
" If no --rules specified, simulation is run against all IPA enabled rules.\n"
" By default there is a IPA-wide limit to number of entries fetched, you can "
"change it\n"
" with --sizelimit option.\n"
"\n"
" If --srchost is specified, it will be ignored. It is left because of "
"compatibility reasons only.\n"
"\n"
"EXAMPLES:\n"
"\n"
"    1. Use all enabled HBAC rules in IPA database to simulate:\n"
"    $ ipa  hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      notmatched: my-second-rule\n"
"      notmatched: my-third-rule\n"
"      notmatched: myrule\n"
"      matched: allow_all\n"
"\n"
"    2. Disable detailed summary of how rules were applied:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --nodetail\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"\n"
"    3. Test explicitly specified HBAC rules:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd           --rules=my-"
"second-rule,myrule\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"    Access granted: False\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"      notmatched: my-second-rule\n"
"      notmatched: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    4. Use all enabled HBAC rules in IPA database + explicitly specified "
"rules:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd           --rules=my-"
"second-rule,myrule --enabled\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      notmatched: my-second-rule\n"
"      notmatched: my-third-rule\n"
"      notmatched: myrule\n"
"      matched: allow_all\n"
"\n"
"    5. Test all disabled HBAC rules in IPA database:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --disabled\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"    Access granted: False\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"      notmatched: new-rule\n"
"\n"
"    6. Test all disabled HBAC rules in IPA database + explicitly specified "
"rules:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd           --rules=my-"
"second-rule,myrule --disabled\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"    Access granted: False\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"      notmatched: my-second-rule\n"
"      notmatched: my-third-rule\n"
"      notmatched: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    7. Test all (enabled and disabled) HBAC rules in IPA database:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd           --enabled "
"--disabled\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      notmatched: my-second-rule\n"
"      notmatched: my-third-rule\n"
"      notmatched: myrule\n"
"      notmatched: new-rule\n"
"      matched: allow_all\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Simula l'ús de controls d'accés basats en l'amfitrió\n"
"\n"
"Les regles HBAC controlen qui pot accedir a quins serveis en quins "
"amfitrions i des d'on.\n"
"Podeu utilitzar HBAC per controlar quins usuaris o grups poden accedir a un "
"servei,\n"
"o grup de serveis, en un amfitrió objectiu.\n"
"\n"
"Atès que aplicar les normes HBAC implica l'ús d'un entorn de producció,\n"
"aquest connector té com a objectiu proporcionar simulació d'avaluació de "
"regles HBAC sense\n"
"tenir accés a l'entorn de producció.\n"
"\n"
" Prova l'usuari que arriba a un servei en un servidor anomenat contra\n"
" regles habilitades existents.\n"
"\n"
" ipa hbactest --user= --host= --service=\n"
"              [--rules]rules-list] [--nodetail] [--enabled] [--disabled]\n"
"              [--srchost  ] [--sizelimit  ]\n"
"\n"
" --user, --host i --service són obligatoris, altres són opcionals.\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --rules simula l'habilitació de les regles i la prova "
"especificades\n"
" l'accés de l'usuari utilitzant només aquestes regles.\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --enabled, totes les regles HBAC habilitades s'afegiran a "
"la simulació\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --disabled, totes les regles HBAC desactivades s'afegiran a "
"la simulació\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --nodetail, no retorneu informació sobre les regles que "
"coincideixen/no coincideixen.\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifiquen --rules i --enabled, apliqueu la simulació a --rules i\n"
" Totes les regles habilitades per l'AFI.\n"
"\n"
" Si no s'especifica --rules, la simulació s'executa contra totes les regles "
"habilitades per l'IPA.\n"
" Per defecte hi ha un límit d'IPA a tot el nombre d'entrades recuperades, "
"podeu canviar-lo\n"
" amb l'opció --sizelimit.\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --srchost, s'ignorarà. Es deixa només per motius de "
"compatibilitat.\n"
"\n"
"EXEMPLES:\n"
"\n"
"    1. Usa totes les regles HBAC habilitades a la base de dades IPA per "
"simular:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      sense coincidència: la meva segona regla\n"
"      no aparellat: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      sense coincidència: myrule\n"
"      coincident: allowall\n"
"\n"
"    2. Desactiva el resum detallat de com s'han aplicat les regles:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --nodetail\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"\n"
"    3. Prova les regles HBAC especificades explícitament:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user,a1a --host,bar --service,sshd --rules,my-second-"
"rule,myrule\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Fals\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      sense coincidència: la meva segona regla\n"
"      sense coincidència: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    4. Usa totes les regles HBAC habilitades a la base de dades IPA + regles "
"especificades explícitament:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user,a1a --host,bar --service,sshd --rules,my-second-"
"rule,myrule --enabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      sense coincidència: la meva segona regla\n"
"      no aparellat: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      sense coincidència: myrule\n"
"      coincident: allowall\n"
"\n"
"    5. Prova totes les regles HBAC desactivades a la base de dades IPA:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --disabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Fals\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      sense coincidència: nova regla\n"
"\n"
"    6. Prova totes les regles HBAC desactivades a la base de dades IPA + "
"regles especificades explícitament:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user,a1a --host,bar --service,sshd --rules,my-second-"
"rule,myrule --disabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Fals\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      sense coincidència: la meva segona regla\n"
"      no aparellat: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      sense coincidència: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    7. Prova totes les regles HBAC (activades i desactivades) a la base de "
"dades IPA:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --enabled --"
"disabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      sense coincidència: la meva segona regla\n"
"      no aparellat: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      sense coincidència: myrule\n"
"      sense coincidència: nova regla\n"
"      coincident: allowall\n"

msgid ""
"\n"
"Password policy\n"
"\n"
"A password policy sets limitations on IPA passwords, including maximum\n"
"lifetime, minimum lifetime, the number of passwords to save in\n"
"history, the number of character classes required (for stronger passwords)\n"
"and the minimum password length.\n"
"\n"
"By default there is a single, global policy for all users. You can also\n"
"create a password policy to apply to a group. Each user is only subject\n"
"to one password policy, either the group policy or the global policy. A\n"
"group policy stands alone; it is not a super-set of the global policy plus\n"
"custom settings.\n"
"\n"
"Each group password policy requires a unique priority setting. If a user\n"
"is in multiple groups that have password policies, this priority determines\n"
"which password policy is applied. A lower value indicates a higher priority\n"
"policy.\n"
"\n"
"Group password policies are automatically removed when the groups they\n"
"are associated with are removed.\n"
"\n"
"EXAMPLES:\n"
"\n"
" Modify the global policy:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-mod --minlength=10\n"
"\n"
" Add a new group password policy:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-add --maxlife=90 --minlife=1 --history=10 --minclasses=3 --"
"minlength=8 --priority=10 localadmins\n"
"\n"
" Display the global password policy:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-show\n"
"\n"
" Display a group password policy:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-show localadmins\n"
"\n"
" Display the policy that would be applied to a given user:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-show --user=tuser1\n"
"\n"
" Modify a group password policy:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-mod --minclasses=2 localadmins\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Política de contrasenyes\n"
"\n"
"Una política de contrasenyes estableix limitacions a les contrasenyes IPA, "
"incloent el màxim\n"
"vida, vida mínima, el nombre de contrasenyes a desar\n"
"historial, el nombre de classes de caràcters requerides (per a contrasenyes "
"més fortes)\n"
"i la longitud mínima de la contrasenya.\n"
"\n"
"Per defecte hi ha una única política global per a tots els usuaris. També "
"pots\n"
"creeu una política de contrasenya per aplicar-la a un grup. Cada usuari "
"només és subjecte\n"
"a una política de contrasenyes, ja sigui la política de grup o la política "
"global. A\n"
"la política de grup està sola; no és un superconjunt de la política global "
"més\n"
"Configuració personalitzada.\n"
"\n"
"Cada política de contrasenyes de grup requereix una configuració de "
"prioritat única. Si un usuari\n"
"és en múltiples grups que tenen polítiques de contrasenyes, aquesta "
"prioritat determina\n"
"quina política de contrasenya s'aplica. Un valor més baix indica una "
"prioritat més alta\n"
"política.\n"
"\n"
"Les polítiques de contrasenyes de grup s'eliminen automàticament quan els "
"grups\n"
"s'associen amb que s'eliminen.\n"
"\n"
"EXEMPLES:\n"
"\n"
" Modificar la política global:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-mod --minlength-10\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix una nova política de contrasenyes de grup:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-add --maxlife p90 --minlifes1 --historys10 --minclassess3 --"
"minlengths8 --priority=10 localadmins\n"
"\n"
" Mostra la política global de contrasenyes:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-show\n"
"\n"
" Mostra una política de contrasenyes de grup:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-show localadmins\n"
"\n"
" Mostra la política que s'aplicarà a un usuari donat:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-show --user=tuser1\n"
"\n"
" Modifica una política de contrasenya de grup:\n"
"   ipa pwpolicy-mod --minclassess2 localadmins\n"

msgid "Results should contain primary key attribute only (\"cn\")"
msgstr "Els resultats han de contenir només l'atribut clau principal (\"cn\")"

msgid "Results should contain primary key attribute only (\"group\")"
msgstr "Els resultats han de contenir només l'atribut clau principal («group»)"

msgid ""
"\n"
"Server configuration\n"
"\n"
"Manage the default values that IPA uses and some of its tuning parameters.\n"
"\n"
"NOTES:\n"
"\n"
"The password notification value (--pwdexpnotify) is stored here so it will\n"
"be replicated. It is not currently used to notify users in advance of an\n"
"expiring password.\n"
"\n"
"Some attributes are read-only, provided only for information purposes. "
"These\n"
"include:\n"
"\n"
"Certificate Subject base: the configured certificate subject base,\n"
"  e.g. O=EXAMPLE.COM.  This is configurable only at install time.\n"
"Password plug-in features: currently defines additional hashes that the\n"
"  password will generate (there may be other conditions).\n"
"\n"
"When setting the order list for mapping SELinux users you may need to\n"
"quote the value so it isn't interpreted by the shell.\n"
"\n"
"EXAMPLES:\n"
"\n"
" Show basic server configuration:\n"
"   ipa config-show\n"
"\n"
" Show all configuration options:\n"
"   ipa config-show --all\n"
"\n"
" Change maximum username length to 99 characters:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --maxusername=99\n"
"\n"
" Increase default time and size limits for maximum IPA server search:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --searchtimelimit=10 --searchrecordslimit=2000\n"
"\n"
" Set default user e-mail domain:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --emaildomain=example.com\n"
"\n"
" Enable migration mode to make \"ipa migrate-ds\" command operational:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --enable-migration=TRUE\n"
"\n"
" Define SELinux user map order:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --ipaselinuxusermaporder='guest_u:s0$xguest_u:s0$user_u:s0-"
"s0:c0.c1023$staff_u:s0-s0:c0.c1023$unconfined_u:s0-s0:c0.c1023'\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Configuració del servidor\n"
"\n"
"Gestiona els valors per defecte que utilitza l'IPA i alguns dels seus "
"paràmetres d'afinació.\n"
"\n"
"NOTES:\n"
"\n"
"El valor de la notificació de contrasenya (--pwdexpnotify) s'emmagatzema "
"aquí, de manera que\n"
"ser replicat. Actualment no s'utilitza per notificar als usuaris amb "
"antelació\n"
"Caduca la contrasenya.\n"
"\n"
"Alguns atributs són només de lectura, proporcionats només amb finalitats "
"d'informació. Aquests\n"
"inclou:\n"
"\n"
"Base de l'assumpte del certificat: la base de l'assumpte del certificat "
"configurat,\n"
"  p. ex. O.EXEMPLE.COM.  Això només es pot configurar en temps "
"d'instal·lació.\n"
"Característiques del connector de contrasenya: actualment defineix resums "
"addicionals que el\n"
"  es generarà la contrasenya (pot haver-hi altres condicions).\n"
"\n"
"En establir la llista de comandes per a mapejar els usuaris de SELinux, és "
"possible que hàgiu de\n"
"citeu el valor perquè no sigui interpretat per l'intèrpret d'ordres.\n"
"\n"
"EXEMPLES:\n"
"\n"
" Mostra la configuració bàsica del servidor:\n"
"   ipa config-show\n"
"\n"
" Mostra totes les opcions de configuració:\n"
"   ipa config-show --all\n"
"\n"
" Canvia la longitud màxima d'usuari a 99 caràcters:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --maxusername=99\n"
"\n"
" Augmenta els límits de temps i mida per defecte per a la cerca màxima del "
"servidor IPA:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --searchtimelimit=10 --searchrecordslimit=2000\n"
"\n"
" Estableix el domini de correu electrònic per defecte de l'usuari:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --emaildomain.example.com\n"
"\n"
" Habilita el mode de migració per a fer operativa l'ordre «ipa migrate-ds»:\n"
"   config-mod --enable-migration=TRUE\n"
"\n"
" Defineix l'ordre del mapa d'usuari de SELinux:\n"
"   ipa config-mod --ipaselinuxusermaporder:'guestu:s0$xguestu:s0-"
"s0:c0.c1023$staffu:s0-s0:c0.c1023$unconfinedu:s0-s0:c0.c1023'\n"

msgid ""
"Maximum amount of time (seconds) for a search (> 0, or -1 for unlimited)"
msgstr ""
"Quantitat màxima de temps (segons) per a una cerca ( 0, 0, o -1 per a "
"il·limitat)"

msgid "Maximum number of records to search (-1 is unlimited)"
msgstr "Nombre màxim de registres a cercar (-1 és il·limitat)"

msgid ""
"\n"
"Domain Name System (DNS)\n"
"\n"
"Manage DNS zone and resource records.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"USING STRUCTURED PER-TYPE OPTIONS\n"
"\n"
"There are many structured DNS RR types where DNS data stored in LDAP server\n"
"is not just a scalar value, for example an IP address or a domain name, but\n"
"a data structure which may be often complex. A good example is a LOC record\n"
"[RFC1876] which consists of many mandatory and optional parts (degrees,\n"
"minutes, seconds of latitude and longitude, altitude or precision).\n"
"\n"
"It may be difficult to manipulate such DNS records without making a mistake\n"
"and entering an invalid value. DNS module provides an abstraction over "
"these\n"
"raw records and allows to manipulate each RR type with specific options. "
"For\n"
"each supported RR type, DNS module provides a standard option to manipulate\n"
"a raw records with format --<rrtype>-rec, e.g. --mx-rec, and special "
"options\n"
"for every part of the RR structure with format --<rrtype>-<partname>, e.g.\n"
"--mx-preference and --mx-exchanger.\n"
"\n"
"When adding a record, either RR specific options or standard option for a "
"raw\n"
"value can be used, they just should not be combined in one add operation. "
"When\n"
"modifying an existing entry, new RR specific options can be used to change\n"
"one part of a DNS record, where the standard option for raw value is used\n"
"to specify the modified value. The following example demonstrates\n"
"a modification of MX record preference from 0 to 1 in a record without\n"
"modifying the exchanger:\n"
"ipa dnsrecord-mod --mx-rec=\"0 mx.example.com.\" --mx-preference=1\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"EXAMPLES:\n"
"\n"
" Add new zone:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add example.com --name-"
"server=ns                                --admin-"
"email=admin@example.com                                --ip-"
"address=10.0.0.1\n"
"\n"
" Add system permission that can be used for per-zone privilege delegation:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add-permission example.com\n"
"\n"
" Modify the zone to allow dynamic updates for hosts own records in realm "
"EXAMPLE.COM:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod example.com --dynamic-update=TRUE\n"
"\n"
"   This is the equivalent of:\n"
"     ipa dnszone-mod example.com --dynamic-update=TRUE       --update-"
"policy=\"grant EXAMPLE.COM krb5-self * A; grant EXAMPLE.COM krb5-self * "
"AAAA; grant EXAMPLE.COM krb5-self * SSHFP;\"\n"
"\n"
" Modify the zone to allow zone transfers for local network only:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod example.com --allow-transfer=10.0.0.0/8\n"
"\n"
" Add new reverse zone specified by network IP address:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add --name-from-ip=80.142.15.0/24                    --name-"
"server=ns.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Add second nameserver for example.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com @ --ns-rec=nameserver2.example.com\n"
"\n"
" Add a mail server for example.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com @ --mx-rec=\"10 mail1\"\n"
"\n"
" Add another record using MX record specific options:\n"
"  ipa dnsrecord-add example.com @ --mx-preference=20 --mx-exchanger=mail2\n"
"\n"
" Add another record using interactive mode (started when dnsrecord-add, "
"dnsrecord-mod,\n"
" or dnsrecord-del are executed with no options):\n"
"  ipa dnsrecord-add example.com @\n"
"  Please choose a type of DNS resource record to be added\n"
"  The most common types for this type of zone are: NS, MX, LOC\n"
"\n"
"  DNS resource record type: MX\n"
"  MX Preference: 30\n"
"  MX Exchanger: mail3\n"
"    Record name: example.com\n"
"    MX record: 10 mail1, 20 mail2, 30 mail3\n"
"    NS record: nameserver.example.com., nameserver2.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Delete previously added nameserver from example.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-del example.com @ --ns-rec=nameserver2.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Add LOC record for example.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com @ --loc-rec=\"49 11 42.4 N 16 36 29.6 E "
"227.64m\"\n"
"\n"
" Add new A record for www.example.com. Create a reverse record in "
"appropriate\n"
" reverse zone as well. In this case a PTR record \"2\" pointing to "
"www.example.com\n"
" will be created in zone 15.142.80.in-addr.arpa.\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com www --a-rec=80.142.15.2 --a-create-reverse\n"
"\n"
" Add new PTR record for www.example.com\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add 15.142.80.in-addr.arpa. 2 --ptr-rec=www.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Add new SRV records for LDAP servers. Three quarters of the requests\n"
" should go to fast.example.com, one quarter to slow.example.com. If neither\n"
" is available, switch to backup.example.com.\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com _ldap._tcp --srv-rec=\"0 3 389 "
"fast.example.com\"\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com _ldap._tcp --srv-rec=\"0 1 389 "
"slow.example.com\"\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com _ldap._tcp --srv-rec=\"1 1 389 "
"backup.example.com\"\n"
"\n"
" The interactive mode can be used for easy modification:\n"
"  ipa dnsrecord-mod example.com _ldap._tcp\n"
"  No option to modify specific record provided.\n"
"  Current DNS record contents:\n"
"\n"
"  SRV record: 0 3 389 fast.example.com, 0 1 389 slow.example.com, 1 1 389 "
"backup.example.com\n"
"\n"
"  Modify SRV record '0 3 389 fast.example.com'? Yes/No (default No):\n"
"  Modify SRV record '0 1 389 slow.example.com'? Yes/No (default No): y\n"
"  SRV Priority [0]:                     (keep the default value)\n"
"  SRV Weight [1]: 2                     (modified value)\n"
"  SRV Port [389]:                       (keep the default value)\n"
"  SRV Target [slow.example.com]:        (keep the default value)\n"
"  1 SRV record skipped. Only one value per DNS record type can be modified "
"at one time.\n"
"    Record name: _ldap._tcp\n"
"    SRV record: 0 3 389 fast.example.com, 1 1 389 backup.example.com, 0 2 "
"389 slow.example.com\n"
"\n"
" After this modification, three fifths of the requests should go to\n"
" fast.example.com and two fifths to slow.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" An example of the interactive mode for dnsrecord-del command:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-del example.com www\n"
"   No option to delete specific record provided.\n"
"   Delete all? Yes/No (default No):     (do not delete all records)\n"
"   Current DNS record contents:\n"
"\n"
"   A record: 1.2.3.4, 11.22.33.44\n"
"\n"
"   Delete A record '1.2.3.4'? Yes/No (default No):\n"
"   Delete A record '11.22.33.44'? Yes/No (default No): y\n"
"     Record name: www\n"
"     A record: 1.2.3.4                  (A record 11.22.33.44 has been "
"deleted)\n"
"\n"
" Show zone example.com:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-show example.com\n"
"\n"
" Find zone with \"example\" in its domain name:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-find example\n"
"\n"
" Find records for resources with \"www\" in their name in zone example.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-find example.com www\n"
"\n"
" Find A records with value 10.10.0.1 in zone example.com\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-find example.com --a-rec=10.10.0.1\n"
"\n"
" Show records for resource www in zone example.com\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-show example.com www\n"
"\n"
" Delegate zone sub.example to another nameserver:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com ns.sub --a-rec=10.0.100.5\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com sub --ns-rec=ns.sub.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" If global forwarder is configured, all requests to sub.example.com will be\n"
" routed through the global forwarder. To change the behavior for "
"example.com\n"
" zone only and forward the request directly to ns.sub.example.com., global\n"
" forwarding may be disabled per-zone:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod example.com --forward-policy=none\n"
"\n"
" Forward all requests for the zone external.com to another nameserver using\n"
" a \"first\" policy (it will send the queries to the selected forwarder and "
"if\n"
" not answered it will use global resolvers):\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add external.com\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod external.com --"
"forwarder=10.20.0.1                                 --forward-policy=first\n"
"\n"
" Delete zone example.com with all resource records:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-del example.com\n"
"\n"
" Resolve a host name to see if it exists (will add default IPA domain\n"
" if one is not included):\n"
"   ipa dns-resolve www.example.com\n"
"   ipa dns-resolve www\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"GLOBAL DNS CONFIGURATION\n"
"\n"
"DNS configuration passed to command line install script is stored in a "
"local\n"
"configuration file on each IPA server where DNS service is configured. "
"These\n"
"local settings can be overridden with a common configuration stored in LDAP\n"
"server:\n"
"\n"
" Show global DNS configuration:\n"
"   ipa dnsconfig-show\n"
"\n"
" Modify global DNS configuration and set a list of global forwarders:\n"
"   ipa dnsconfig-mod --forwarder=10.0.0.1\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Sistema de Noms de Domini (DNS)\n"
"\n"
"Gestiona la zona DNS i els registres de recursos.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"ÚS D'OPCIONS ESTRUCTURADES PER TIPUS\n"
"\n"
"Hi ha molts tipus d'RR DNS estructurats on les dades DNS s'emmagatzemen al "
"servidor LDAP\n"
"no és només un valor escalar, per exemple una adreça IP o un nom de domini, "
"sinó\n"
"Una estructura de dades que sovint pot ser complexa. Un bon exemple és un "
"registre LOC\n"
"[RFC1876] que consta de moltes parts obligatòries i opcionals (graus,\n"
"minuts, segons de latitud i longitud, altitud o precisió).\n"
"\n"
"Pot ser difícil manipular aquests registres DNS sense cometre un error\n"
"i introduir un valor no vàlid. El mòdul DNS proporciona una abstracció sobre "
"aquests\n"
"registres en brut i permet manipular cada tipus de RR amb opcions "
"específiques. Per\n"
"Cada tipus RR suportat, el mòdul DNS proporciona una opció estàndard per "
"manipular\n"
"un registre RAW amb format --<rrtype>-rec, p. ex. --mx-rec, i opcions "
"especials\n"
"per a cada part de l'estructura RR amb format --<rrtype>-<partname>, p. "
"ex. --mx-preference i --mx-exchanger.\n"
"\n"
"Quan s'afegeix un registre, ja siguin opcions específiques de RR o opcions "
"estàndard per a un RAW\n"
"es pot utilitzar el valor, simplement no s'han de combinar en una operació "
"d'addició. Quan\n"
"modificant una entrada existent, es poden utilitzar noves opcions "
"específiques de RR per a canviar\n"
"una part d'un registre DNS, on s'utilitza l'opció estàndard per al valor "
"RAW\n"
"per a especificar el valor modificat. L'exemple següent demostra\n"
"una modificació de la preferència del registre MX de 0 a 1 en un registre "
"sense\n"
"modificant l'intercanviador:\n"
"ipa dnsrecord-mod --mx-rec.\"\"0 mx.example.com.\" --mx-preference11\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"EXEMPLES:\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix una zona nova:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add example.com --name-server.ns --admin-"
"email.admin.example.com --ip-address.10.0.0.1\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix el permís del sistema que es pot utilitzar per a la delegació de "
"privilegis per zona:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add-permission example.com\n"
"\n"
" Modifiqueu la zona per a permetre actualitzacions dinàmiques per als "
"servidors de registres propis al realm EXAMPLE.COM:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod example.com --dynamic-update=TRUE\n"
"\n"
"   Aquest és l'equivalent a:\n"
"     ipa dnszone-mod example.com --dynamic-update.TRUE --update-"
"policy.\"grant EXAMPLE.COM krb5-self * A; grant EXAMPLE.COM krb5-self * "
"AAAA; grant EXAMPLE.COM krb5-self * SSHFP;\"\n"
"\n"
" Modifica la zona per permetre transferències de zona només per a la xarxa "
"local:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod example.com --allow-transfer=10.0.0.0/8\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix una nova zona inversa especificada per l'adreça IP de la xarxa:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add --name-from-ip.80.142.15.0/24 --name-"
"server.ns.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix un servidor de segon nom per exemple.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com   --ns-rec.nameserver2.example.com\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix un servidor de correu per exemple.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com \" --mx-rec\"\"10 mail1\"\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix un altre registre utilitzant les opcions específiques del registre "
"MX:\n"
"  ipa dnsrecord-add example.com   --mx-preference=20 --mx-exchanger.mail2\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix un altre registre utilitzant el mode interactiu (iniciat quan "
"dnsrecord-add, dnsrecord-mod,\n"
" o dnsrecord-del s'executa sense opcions):\n"
"  ipa dnsrecord-add example.com\n"
"  Si us plau, trieu un tipus de registre de recursos DNS a afegir\n"
"  Els tipus més comuns per a aquest tipus de zones són: NS, MX, LOC\n"
"\n"
"  Tipus de registre de recurs DNS: MX\n"
"  Preferència MX: 30\n"
"  Intercanviador MX: mail3\n"
"    Nom del registre: example.com\n"
"    Registre MX: 10 mail1, 20 mail2, 30 mail3\n"
"    Registre NS: nameserver.example.com., nameserver2.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Suprimeix el servidor de noms afegit prèviament d'exemple.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-del example.com . --ns-rec.nameserver2.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix un registre LOC per exemple.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com \" --loc-rec\"\"49 11 42.4 N 16 36 29.6 E "
"227.64m\"\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix un nou registre A per a www.example.com. Crea un registre invers "
"apropiat\n"
" Zona inversa també. En aquest cas un registre PTR \"2\" apuntant a "
"www.example.com\n"
" es crearà a la zona 15.142.80.in-addr.arpa.\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com www --a-rec.80.142.15.2 --a-create-reverse\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix un registre PTR nou a www.example.com\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add 15.142.80.in-addr.arpa. 2 --ptr-rec.www.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Afegeix registres SRV nous per als servidors LDAP. Tres quartes parts de "
"les sol·licituds\n"
" hauria d'anar a fast.example.com, un quart a slow.example.com. Si cap\n"
" està disponible, commuteu a backup.example.com.\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com ldap.tcp --srv-rec\"\"0 3 389 "
"fast.example.com\"\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com ldap.tcp --srv-rec\"\"0 1 389 "
"slow.example.com\"\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com ldap.tcp --srv-rec\"\"1 1 389 "
"backup.example.com\"\n"
"\n"
" El mode interactiu es pot utilitzar per a una fàcil modificació:\n"
"  ipa dnsrecord-mod example.com ldap.tcp\n"
"  No s'ha proporcionat cap opció per modificar el registre específic.\n"
"  Contingut del registre DNS actual:\n"
"\n"
"  Registre SRV: 0 3 389 fast.example.com, 0 1 389 slow.example.com, 1 1 389 "
"backup.example.com\n"
"\n"
"  Modifica el registre SRV '0 3 389 fast.example.com'? Sí/No (predeterminat "
"No):\n"
"  Modifica el registre SRV '0 1 389 slow.example.com'? Sí/No (predeterminat "
"No): y\n"
"  Prioritat SRV [0]: (manté el valor per defecte)\n"
"  Pes SRV [1]: 2 (valor modificat)\n"
"  Port SRV [389]: (manté el valor per defecte)\n"
"  Objectiu SRV [slow.example.com]: (manté el valor per defecte)\n"
"  S'ha omès 1 registre SRV. Només es pot modificar un valor per tipus de "
"registre DNS alhora.\n"
"    Nom del registre: ldap.tcp\n"
"    Registre SRV: 0 3 389 fast.example.com, 1 1 389 backup.example.com, 0 2 "
"389 slow.example.com\n"
"\n"
" Després d'aquesta modificació, tres cinquenes parts de les sol·licituds han "
"d'anar a\n"
" fast.example.com i dues quintes slow.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Un exemple del mode interactiu per a l'ordre dnsrecord-del:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-del example.com www\n"
"   No s'ha proporcionat cap opció per suprimir el registre específic.\n"
"   Voleu suprimir-ho tot? Sí/No (predeterminat No): (no esborris tots els "
"registres)\n"
"   Contingut del registre DNS actual:\n"
"\n"
"   Un registre: 1.2.3.4, 11.22.33.44\n"
"\n"
"   Voleu suprimir un registre '1.2.3.4'? Sí/No (predeterminat No):\n"
"   Voleu suprimir un registre '11.22.33.44'? Sí/No (predeterminat No): y\n"
"     Nom del registre: www\n"
"     Un registre: 1.2.3.4 (S'ha eliminat un registre 11.22.33.44)\n"
"\n"
" Mostra l'exemple de la zona.com:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-show example.com\n"
"\n"
" Troba la zona amb \"exemple\" en el seu nom de domini:\n"
"   Exemple dnszone-find d'ipa\n"
"\n"
" Trobar registres de recursos amb \"www\" en el seu nom a zona exemple.com:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-find example.com www\n"
"\n"
" Cerca registres amb valor 10.10.0.1 a zone example.com\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-find example.com --a-rec.10.10.0.1\n"
"\n"
" Mostra els registres del recurs www a zone example.com\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-show example.com www\n"
"\n"
" Delega la zona sub.example a un altre servidor de noms:\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com ns.sub --a-rec.10.0.100.5\n"
"   ipa dnsrecord-add example.com sub --ns-rec.ns.sub.example.com.\n"
"\n"
" Si el remitent global està configurat, totes les sol·licituds a "
"sub.example.com seran\n"
" Encaminada a través del davanter global. Per a canviar el comportament, per "
"exemple.com\n"
" només zona i reenvia la sol·licitud directament a ns.sub.example.com., "
"global\n"
" El reenviament es pot desactivar per zona:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod example.com --forward-policy=none\n"
"\n"
" Reenvia totes les sol·licituds de la zona external.com a un altre servidor "
"de noms que utilitzi\n"
" una política \"primera\" (enviarà les consultes al remitent seleccionat i "
"si\n"
" no contestat s'utilitzaran resoledors globals):\n"
"   ipa dnszone-add external.com\n"
"   ipa dnszone-mod external.com --forwarder.10.20.0.1 --forward-"
"policy.first\n"
"\n"
" Suprimeix zone example.com amb tots els registres de recursos:\n"
"   ipa dnszone-del example.com\n"
"\n"
" Resol un nom d'amfitrió per veure si existeix (afegirà el domini IPA per "
"defecte\n"
" si no s'inclou:\n"
"   ipa dns-resolve www.example.com\n"
"   ipa dns-resolve www\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"CONFIGURACIÓ GLOBAL DEL DNS\n"
"\n"
"La configuració DNS passada a l'script d'instal·lació de la línia d'ordres "
"s'emmagatzema en un local\n"
"fitxer de configuració a cada servidor IPA on es configura el servei DNS. "
"Aquests\n"
"els paràmetres locals es poden anul·lar amb una configuració comuna "
"emmagatzemada a LDAP\n"
"servidor:\n"
"\n"
" Mostra la configuració global del DNS:\n"
"   ipa dnsconfig-show\n"
"\n"
" Modifica la configuració global del DNS i estableix una llista de remitents "
"globals:\n"
"   ipa dnsconfig-mod --forwarder.10.0.0.1\n"

