msgid ""
"\n"
"Simulate use of Host-based access controls\n"
"\n"
"HBAC rules control who can access what services on what hosts.\n"
"You can use HBAC to control which users or groups can access a service,\n"
"or group of services, on a target host.\n"
"\n"
"Since applying HBAC rules implies use of a production environment,\n"
"this plugin aims to provide simulation of HBAC rules evaluation without\n"
"having access to the production environment.\n"
"\n"
" Test user coming to a service on a named host against\n"
" existing enabled rules.\n"
"\n"
" ipa hbactest --user= --host= --service=\n"
"              [--rules=rules-list] [--nodetail] [--enabled] [--disabled]\n"
"              [--sizelimit= ]\n"
"\n"
" --user, --host, and --service are mandatory, others are optional.\n"
"\n"
" If --rules is specified simulate enabling of the specified rules and test\n"
" the login of the user using only these rules.\n"
"\n"
" If --enabled is specified, all enabled HBAC rules will be added to "
"simulation\n"
"\n"
" If --disabled is specified, all disabled HBAC rules will be added to "
"simulation\n"
"\n"
" If --nodetail is specified, do not return information about rules matched/"
"not matched.\n"
"\n"
" If both --rules and --enabled are specified, apply simulation to --rules "
"_and_\n"
" all IPA enabled rules.\n"
"\n"
" If no --rules specified, simulation is run against all IPA enabled rules.\n"
" By default there is a IPA-wide limit to number of entries fetched, you can "
"change it\n"
" with --sizelimit option.\n"
"\n"
"EXAMPLES:\n"
"\n"
"    1. Use all enabled HBAC rules in IPA database to simulate:\n"
"    $ ipa  hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-second-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-third-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: myrule\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"\n"
"    2. Disable detailed summary of how rules were applied:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --nodetail\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"\n"
"    3. Test explicitly specified HBAC rules:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --rules=myrule --rules=my-second-rule\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"    Access granted: False\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-second-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    4. Use all enabled HBAC rules in IPA database + explicitly specified "
"rules:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --rules=myrule --rules=my-second-rule --enabled\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-second-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-third-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: myrule\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"\n"
"    5. Test all disabled HBAC rules in IPA database:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --disabled\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"    Access granted: False\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"      Not matched rules: new-rule\n"
"\n"
"    6. Test all disabled HBAC rules in IPA database + explicitly specified "
"rules:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --rules=myrule --rules=my-second-rule --disabled\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"    Access granted: False\n"
"    ---------------------\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-second-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-third-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    7. Test all (enabled and disabled) HBAC rules in IPA database:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --enabled --disabled\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-second-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: my-third-rule\n"
"      Not matched rules: myrule\n"
"      Not matched rules: new-rule\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"HBACTEST AND TRUSTED DOMAINS\n"
"\n"
"When an external trusted domain is configured in IPA, HBAC rules are also "
"applied\n"
"on users accessing IPA resources from the trusted domain. Trusted domain "
"users and\n"
"groups (and their SIDs) can be then assigned to external groups which can "
"be\n"
"members of POSIX groups in IPA which can be used in HBAC rules and thus "
"allowing\n"
"access to resources protected by the HBAC system.\n"
"\n"
"hbactest plugin is capable of testing access for both local IPA users and "
"users\n"
"from the trusted domains, either by a fully qualified user name or by user "
"SID.\n"
"Such user names need to have a trusted domain specified as a short name\n"
"(DOMAIN\\Administrator) or with a user principal name (UPN), "
"Administrator@ad.test.\n"
"\n"
"Please note that hbactest executed with a trusted domain user as --user "
"parameter\n"
"can be only run by members of \"trust admins\" group.\n"
"\n"
"EXAMPLES:\n"
"\n"
"    1. Test if a user from a trusted domain specified by its shortname "
"matches any\n"
"       rule:\n"
"\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user 'DOMAIN\\Administrator' --host `hostname` --"
"service sshd\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"      Matched rules: can_login\n"
"\n"
"    2. Test if a user from a trusted domain specified by its domain name "
"matches\n"
"       any rule:\n"
"\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user 'Administrator@domain.com' --host `hostname` --"
"service sshd\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"      Matched rules: can_login\n"
"\n"
"    3. Test if a user from a trusted domain specified by its SID matches any "
"rule:\n"
"\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user S-1-5-21-3035198329-144811719-1378114514-500 \\\n"
"            --host `hostname` --service sshd\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"      Matched rules: can_login\n"
"\n"
"    4. Test if other user from a trusted domain specified by its SID matches "
"any rule:\n"
"\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user S-1-5-21-3035198329-144811719-1378114514-1203 \\\n"
"            --host `hostname` --service sshd\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"      Not matched rules: can_login\n"
"\n"
"   5. Test if other user from a trusted domain specified by its shortname "
"matches\n"
"       any rule:\n"
"\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user 'DOMAIN\\Otheruser' --host `hostname` --service "
"sshd\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"    Access granted: True\n"
"    --------------------\n"
"      Matched rules: allow_all\n"
"      Not matched rules: can_login\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Simula l'ús de controls d'accés basats en l'amfitrió\n"
"\n"
"Les regles HBAC controlen qui pot accedir a quins serveis en quins "
"amfitrions.\n"
"Podeu utilitzar HBAC per controlar quins usuaris o grups poden accedir a un "
"servei,\n"
"o grup de serveis, en un amfitrió objectiu.\n"
"\n"
"Atès que aplicar les normes HBAC implica l'ús d'un entorn de producció,\n"
"aquest connector té com a objectiu proporcionar simulació d'avaluació de "
"regles HBAC sense\n"
"tenir accés a l'entorn de producció.\n"
"\n"
" Prova l'usuari que arriba a un servei en un servidor anomenat contra\n"
" regles habilitades existents.\n"
"\n"
" ipa hbactest --user= --host= --service=\n"
"              [--rules]rules-list] [--nodetail] [--enabled] [--disabled]\n"
"              [--sizelimit ]\n"
"\n"
" --user, --host i --service són obligatoris, altres són opcionals.\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --rules simula l'habilitació de les regles i la prova "
"especificades\n"
" l'accés de l'usuari utilitzant només aquestes regles.\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --enabled, totes les regles HBAC habilitades s'afegiran a "
"la simulació\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --disabled, totes les regles HBAC desactivades s'afegiran a "
"la simulació\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifica --nodetail, no retorneu informació sobre les regles que "
"coincideixen/no coincideixen.\n"
"\n"
" Si s'especifiquen --rules i --enabled, apliqueu la simulació a --rules i\n"
" Totes les regles habilitades per l'AFI.\n"
"\n"
" Si no s'especifica --rules, la simulació s'executa contra totes les regles "
"habilitades per l'IPA.\n"
" Per defecte hi ha un límit d'IPA a tot el nombre d'entrades recuperades, "
"podeu canviar-lo\n"
" amb l'opció --sizelimit.\n"
"\n"
"EXEMPLES:\n"
"\n"
"    1. Usa totes les regles HBAC habilitades a la base de dades IPA per "
"simular:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva segona regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: myrule\n"
"      Regles coincidents: allowall\n"
"\n"
"    2. Desactiva el resum detallat de com s'han aplicat les regles:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --nodetail\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"\n"
"    3. Prova les regles HBAC especificades explícitament:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --rules-myrule --rules-my-second-rule\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Fals\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva segona regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    4. Usa totes les regles HBAC habilitades a la base de dades IPA + regles "
"especificades explícitament:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --rules-myrule --rules-my-second-rule --enabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva segona regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: myrule\n"
"      Regles coincidents: allowall\n"
"\n"
"    5. Prova totes les regles HBAC desactivades a la base de dades IPA:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd --disabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Fals\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: nova regla\n"
"\n"
"    6. Prova totes les regles HBAC desactivades a la base de dades IPA + "
"regles especificades explícitament:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --rules-myrule --rules-my-second-rule --disabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Fals\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva segona regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: myrule\n"
"\n"
"    7. Prova totes les regles HBAC (activades i desactivades) a la base de "
"dades IPA:\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user=a1a --host=bar --service=sshd \\\n"
"          --enabled --disabled\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva segona regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: la meva tercera regla\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: myrule\n"
"      Regles no coincidents: nova regla\n"
"      Regles coincidents: allowall\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"HBACTEST I DOMINIS DE CONFIANÇA\n"
"\n"
"Quan un domini extern de confiança està configurat en IPA, també s'apliquen "
"les regles HBAC\n"
"als usuaris que accedeixen als recursos IPA des del domini de confiança. "
"Usuaris de domini de confiança i\n"
"els grups (i els seus SID) es poden assignar a grups externs que poden ser\n"
"membres dels grups POSIX en IPA que es poden utilitzar en les regles HBAC i, "
"per tant, permetent\n"
"Accés als recursos protegits pel sistema HBAC.\n"
"\n"
"El connector hbactest és capaç de provar l'accés tant per als usuaris locals "
"de l'IPA com per als usuaris\n"
"dels dominis de confiança, ja sigui per un nom d'usuari totalment qualificat "
"o per l'usuari SID.\n"
"Aquests noms d'usuari necessiten tenir un domini de confiança especificat "
"com a nom curt\n"
"(DOMAIN\\Administrator) o amb un nom principal d'usuari (UPN), "
"Administrator.ad.test.\n"
"\n"
"Tingueu en compte que hbactest s'ha executat amb un usuari de domini de "
"confiança com a paràmetre --user\n"
"només pot ser dirigit per membres del grup \"administradors de confiança\".\n"
"\n"
"EXEMPLES:\n"
"\n"
"    1. Prova si un usuari d'un domini de confiança especificat pel seu nom "
"curt coincideix amb qualsevol\n"
"       regla:\n"
"\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user 'DOMAIN\\Administrator' --host 'hostname' --"
"service sshd\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"    Accés concedit: Cert\n"
"    ---------------\n"
"      Regles coincidents: allowall\n"
"      Regles coincidents: canlogin\n"
"\n"
"    2. Prova si un usuari d'un domini de confiança especificat pel seu nom "
"de domini coincideix\n"
"       qualsevol regla:\n"
"\n"
"    $ ipa hbactest --user 'Administrator.domain.com' --host 'hostname` --"
"service sshd\n"
"    ---------------\n"
